## 4. Agent-by-Agent Summary

| Agent | Focus | Key Finding | Verdict |
|-------|-------|-------------|---------|
| **0 (Engine)** | Z-score bug fix + reconciliation | Phase 4 used in-sample z (buggy: 10 trades -3.24%). Correct rolling z: 12 trades +4.15%. Walk-forward: +8.03% avg over 14 folds. Null test: 90.2th percentile (below 95th gate). 2x cost robust: +3.45%. | Fixed critical bug. Correct z-score is canonical. |
| **1 (Execution)** | Fill type comparison | MOO is best (+4.15% avg). Limit orders hurt (-1.74% penalty). MOC marginal (+4.93% but 2 fewer trades). 9:30 open optimal fill. | Keep MOO. No change. |
| **2 (Overnight/Intraday)** | PnL decomposition | 85% of PnL is intraday. AM session dominant. LONG signals: negative overnight but strong intraday. Regime-robust: worked in both overnight regimes. | Edge is intraday mean-reversion, not overnight drift. |
| **3 (Events)** | Event proximity effect | Near-event vs far-event: p=0.91 (no difference). Event avoidance gate costs -0.46% avg by reducing n. Edge is broad spread mean-reversion, not event-driven. | No event filter. Keep all trades. |
| **4 (S/R Levels)** | Support/resistance gates | Binary S/R gate: p=0.42 (no signal). Proximity weighting (alpha 0.5-2.0): dilutes returns or no effect. ATR-based levels don't improve z-score entry. | No S/R overlay. Keep raw z-score entry. |
| **5 (Multi-Factor)** | Hedge construction | ARKG-only is best. Adding XBI, IBB, SPY, PCA, or Kalman all reduce OOS performance. R-squared vs performance: r=-0.763 (more factors = weaker signal). Over-hedging removes the tradeable idiosyncratic component. | ARKG-only hedge. Adding factors hurts. |
| **6 (Attention/Positioning)** | Signal quality proxies | Volume gate: reduces n from 12 to 9, marginal avg lift (+0.27%). VIX gate: kills all trades (0 remaining). Squeeze, sector flow: p>0.10. n=12 OOS is too small for subsetting. | No proxy filters. All p>0.10. |
| **7 (Exit Engineering)** | Alternative exits | All trailing stops worse than z-exit (T1-T4: +0.76% to +3.37% vs baseline +4.15%). Partial exits: no improvement. Z-exit 0.5 optimal in-sample. Only finding: max_hold=20d shows +1.3% OOS improvement with 15/17 walk-forward folds positive. | Keep z-exit 0.5. Consider max_hold=20d. |

